{"a1":[{"k":"title","cap":"Every Subset","say":"Let's solve Every Subset, using the Backtracking approach.","card":{"title":"Every Subset","sub":"Backtracking · Medium","pattern":"backtracking"}},{"k":"problem","cap":"nums has distinct integers. Return every possible subset (the power set), in any order, with no duplicates.","card":{"lines":["nums has distinct integers. Return every possible subset (the power set), in any order, with no duplicates."]}},{"k":"example","cap":"For example, with nums = [1,2,3], the answer is [[],[1],[2],[1,2],[3],[1,3],[2,3],[1,2,3]].","say":"For example, with nums equals 1, 2, 3, the answer is, 1, 2, 1, 2, 3, 1, 3, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3.","card":{"lines":["Input: nums = [1,2,3]","Output: [[],[1],[2],[1,2],[3],[1,3],[2,3],[1,2,3]]"]}},{"k":"idea","cap":"Build subsets one decision at a time. At each step record the current subset, then try adding each remaining element, explore deeper, and remove it again (backtrack) before trying the next one.","card":{"pattern":"backtracking","name":"Backtracking"}},{"k":"trace","cap":"Let's walk through it with nums = [1,2,3].","say":"Let's walk through it with nums equals 1, 2, 3.","st":{"arrays":[{"n":"nums","v":["1","2","3"],"p":[{"l":"start","i":0}]}],"out":{"n":"current","v":[]}}},{"k":"step","cap":"Record the subset [].","say":"Record the subset.","ln":{"python":5,"java":9},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"nums","v":["1","2","3"],"p":[{"l":"start","i":0}]}],"out":{"n":"current","v":[]}}},{"k":"step","cap":"Record the subset [1].","say":"Record the subset 1.","ln":{"python":5,"java":9},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"nums","v":["1","2","3"],"p":[{"l":"start","i":1}]}],"out":{"n":"current","v":["1"]}}},{"k":"step","cap":"Record the subset [1, 2].","say":"Record the subset 1, 2.","ln":{"python":5,"java":9},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"nums","v":["1","2","3"],"p":[{"l":"start","i":2}]}],"out":{"n":"current","v":["1","2"]}}},{"k":"step","cap":"Record the subset [1, 2, 3].","say":"Record the subset 1, 2, 3.","ln":{"python":5,"java":9},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"nums","v":["1","2","3"],"p":[{"l":"start","i":3}]}],"out":{"n":"current","v":["1","2","3"]}}},{"k":"step","cap":"Record the subset [1, 3].","say":"Record the subset 1, 3.","ln":{"python":5,"java":9},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"nums","v":["1","2","3"],"p":[{"l":"start","i":3}]}],"out":{"n":"current","v":["1","3"]}}},{"k":"step","cap":"Record the subset [2].","say":"Record the subset 2.","ln":{"python":5,"java":9},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"nums","v":["1","2","3"],"p":[{"l":"start","i":2}]}],"out":{"n":"current","v":["2"]}}},{"k":"step","cap":"Record the subset [2, 3].","say":"Record the subset 2, 3.","ln":{"python":5,"java":9},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"nums","v":["1","2","3"],"p":[{"l":"start","i":3}]}],"out":{"n":"current","v":["2","3"]}}},{"k":"step","cap":"Record the subset [3].","say":"Record the subset 3.","ln":{"python":5,"java":9},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"nums","v":["1","2","3"],"p":[{"l":"start","i":3}]}],"out":{"n":"current","v":["3"]}}},{"k":"done","cap":"The answer is [[],[1],[1,2],[1,2,3],[1,3],[2],[2,3],[3]].","say":"The answer is, 1, 1, 2, 1, 2, 3, 1, 3, 2, 2, 3, 3.","st":{"arrays":[{"n":"nums","v":["1","2","3"],"p":[{"l":"start","i":3}]}],"out":{"n":"current","v":["3"]}}},{"k":"complexity","cap":"Time complexity is O(n · 2ⁿ) and extra space is O(n).","say":"Time complexity is O of n times 2 to the n and extra space is O of n.","card":{"time":"O(n · 2ⁿ)","space":"O(n)"}},{"k":"outro","cap":"That's the Backtracking approach. Now try writing it yourself, in Java or Python!"}]}